// Title: Creation of a Local Hidden User Account by Registry
// Sigma ID: 460479f3-80b7-42da-9c43-2cc1d54dbccd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-05-03 | Modified: 2025-10-31
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1136.001
// Description: Sysmon registry detection of a local hidden user account.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/SBousseaden/status/1387530414185664538
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_add_local_hidden_user.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SAM\\SAM\\Domains\\Account\\Users\\Names.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "$\\(Default)" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\lsass.exe"
